// A parsed schema as RUNTIME description: `StateDef` -> `@tutuca.SchemaInfo`.
//
// A sub-package rather than a file in `statedef`, and the reason is stated in
// `statedef/types.mbt`: `ty_info_src` returns TEXT because "statedef stays a
// pure text-in/text-out package, and importing core here would drag
// `@tutuca.Value` in for the sake of one enum". That rule is right and it
// stays; what changes is that there is now a consumer who needs the VALUE and
// not the source of it.
//
// The consumer is a runtime. `viewgen` emits `ty_info_src` into a generated
// module and the MoonBit compiler turns it into a `TyInfo` — which works
// because there is a compiler. A card is mounted in a browser with no
// generator and no compiler anywhere in the payload, so the same projection
// has to be available as a function. One declaration, two ways of reaching the
// same description, and the emitter and this file are checked against each
// other by the test suite here.
import {
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/statedef",
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/core" @tutuca,
  // For `zero_of_ref`: the block language parses a `new`'s type as a NAME,
  // since it sees no schema. This is where the two halves meet, and it is a
  // leaf import — `tscript` depends on neither package.
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/tscript",
}
